### 4. ⚠️ Information Disclosure (OWASP A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration)

**Severity:** HIGH
**Risk:** Detailed error messages can reveal internal system information.

**Finding:** No custom error handling, which returns default Express error pages.

**Recommended Solution:** Implement error handling middleware

```javascript
// Custom error response utility
function sendErrorResponse(res, statusCode, message, details = null) {
  const errorResponse = {
    error: message
  };

  // Only log and return details in development
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' && details) {
    errorResponse.details = details;
  }

  res.status(statusCode).json(errorResponse);
  console.error(`[${statusCode}] ${message}`, details || '');
}

// Global error handling middleware
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log error with stack trace in development
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
    console.error('Error:', err); // ⚠️ Don't expose stack traces to users!
  }

  // Remove sensitive fields from error
  const safeErrorDetails = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? err.stack : null;

  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    error: err.message || 'Internal server error'
  });
});

// 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => {
  sendErrorResponse(res, 404, 'Endpoint not found', {
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method
  });
});

// Performance error handler
app.use('/slow', (req, res, next) => {
  // Simulate slow operation with timeout
  let requestTime = Date.now();
  res.on('finish', () => {
    const duration = Date.now() - requestTime;
    if (duration > 1000) {
      console.warn(`Slow response: ${req.path} took ${duration}ms`);
    }
  });
  next();
});
```

