### 5. ⚠️ No Rate Limiting (OWASP A04:2021 - Insecure Design)

**Severity:** MEDIUM-HIGH
**Risk:** Application vulnerable to brute force attacks, denial of service.

**Finding:** No rate limiting on any endpoints.

**Recommended Solution:** Implement rate limiting

```javascript
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const RedisStore = require('rate-limit-redis');
const redis = require('redis');

// Create Redis client for rate limiting
const redisClient = redis.createClient({
  url: process.env.REDIS_URL || 'redis://localhost:6379',
  password: process.env.REDIS_PASSWORD
});

// General rate limiter - prevents abuse
const generalLimiter = rateLimit({
  store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient }),
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100, // Limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
  message: 'Too many requests from this IP, please try again later',
  standardHeaders: true,
  legacyHeaders: false,
});

// Login rate limiter - stricter limits
const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient }),
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 5, // Limit to 5 login attempts per window
  message: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later',
  skipSuccessfulRequests: true, // Don't count successful requests
});

// Apply rate limiting
app.use(generalLimiter); // Apply to all routes

app.post('/login', loginLimiter, async (req, res) => {
  // Login code here
});

// Admin routes should have stricter limits
app.use('/admin',
  authenticateToken,
  rateLimit({
    store: new RedisStore({ client: redisClient }),
    windowMs: 60 * 1000, // 1 minute
    max: 30, // 30 requests per minute for admin endpoints
  }),
  requireRole([ROLES.ADMIN])
);

// Apply to all routes after authentication
const authenticatedRoutes = express.Router();
authenticatedRoutes.use(authenticateToken);
// Add authenticated route handlers to authenticatedRoutes
```

